{"id":"2579f81f77b3d245","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-thm-pcf-structure.md","title":"PCF Structure for Progressive Sets","display":"thm-pcf-structure — PCF Structure for Progressive Sets","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-pcf-structure","aliases":["58-thm-pcf-structure"],"display":"thm-pcf-structure — PCF Structure for Progressive Sets","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-shelah-pcf.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-pcf-structure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-pcf-structure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-pcf-structure — PCF Structure for Progressive Sets"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3f02dbef75736ea3\" href=\"?note=3f02dbef75736ea3\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-shelah-pcf.md\">../batch17/58-df-shelah-pcf.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-pcf-structure-—-PCF-Structure-Theorem\">thm-pcf-structure — PCF Structure Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> (set of regular cardinals)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\neq\\varnothing\">\\(A\\neq\\varnothing\\)</span>, every member of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is regular, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|A|&lt;\\min A\">\\(|A|&lt;\\min A\\)</span> (the progressive hypothesis)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> (regular-cardinal predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pcf}\">\\(\\mathrm{pcf}\\)</span> (possible-cofinality operator)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf-structure} \\vdash \\Bigl(A\\neq\\varnothing\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\\Bigr)\\to\\Bigl(A\\subseteq\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\mu)\\bigr)\\land|\\mathrm{pcf}(A)|\\leq2^{|A|}\\land\\exists\\lambda\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf-structure} \\vdash \\Bigl(A\\neq\\varnothing\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\\Bigr)\\to\\Bigl(A\\subseteq\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\mu)\\bigr)\\land|\\mathrm{pcf}(A)|\\leq2^{|A|}\\land\\exists\\lambda\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The input to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pcf}\">\\(\\mathrm{pcf}\\)</span> is a progressive set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> of regular cardinals, not a bare singular cardinal.</li>\n<li>The progressive condition is expanded in the theorem instead of invoking a predicate that no dependency defines.</li>\n<li>The final conjunct states that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\">\\(\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\)</span> has a maximum.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-pcf-structure-—-PCF-Structure-Theorem","text":"thm-pcf-structure — PCF Structure Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-shelah-pcf.md","status":"resolved","id":"3f02dbef75736ea3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-shelah-pcf.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"A\\neq\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"|A|<\\min A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{pcf}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf-structure} \\vdash \\Bigl(A\\neq\\varnothing\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|<\\min A\\Bigr)\\to\\Bigl(A\\subseteq\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\mu)\\bigr)\\land|\\mathrm{pcf}(A)|\\leq2^{|A|}\\land\\exists\\lambda\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\mathrm{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{pcf}","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{pcf}(A)","display":false}],"bytes":1353,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4349","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-thm-pcf-structure.md|58-thm-pcf-structure]]（batch11）"}],"outgoing":["3f02d